cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its aggregate results, please cite it as below,
  together with the accompanying article.
type: software
title: HETUS household electricity profiling pipeline
abstract: >-
  Python pipeline that derives profiles of the activity-associated appliance
  load of households at 10-minute resolution from the 2010 wave of the
  Harmonised European Time Use Surveys (HETUS) for 15 countries, clusters them
  globally, by day type, by country and by country and day type, validates the
  clusters statistically, and propagates 21 modelling choices through the whole
  pipeline in a global sensitivity analysis. The outputs folder holds the
  aggregate results behind the accompanying article, under Eurostat's
  publication rules for HETUS. The HETUS microdata are Eurostat scientific use
  files and are not included.
